GL buffer updates that discard do not wait for the GPU.

OutRun 2006 races on the RG DS (Mali-G52, Mesa 25.0): the presentation quad's vertex buffer is rewritten every frame
with UPDATE_DISCARD while the last frame's final draw still uses it. glBufferSubData made Panfrost wait in
panfrost_bo_wait until that whole frame had left the GPU: 16 % of the GL thread's wall time by sampling. Mapping
with GL_MAP_INVALIDATE_BUFFER_BIT gets fresh storage instead: 4585 frames in 90 s against 4334 and 4318
(RGDS_GL_DISCARD_UPDATES=0 keeps the wait).

